WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.956
If it connects to the internet, it can be hacked. Routers, cameras, smart TVs, even the shop's payment speaker.

2
00:00:09.256 --> 00:00:16.317
Many come with a factory password, like admin, admin. Criminals search the internet for exactly those.

3
00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:26.431
At home, change the router password on day one. Use WPA2 or WPA3, and switch off WPS and remote management.

4
00:00:26.731 --> 00:00:33.247
Keep its firmware updated. Outdated routers can be taken over, and send you to fake bank sites.

5
00:00:33.647 --> 00:00:42.704
A camera on its default password can be watched by strangers. Change it, turn on two-step login, and never place one in a private space.

6
00:00:43.004 --> 00:00:47.895
My shop camera came from the market. No brand, no updates.

7
00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:52.406
Buy brands that give security updates, and avoid unbranded cameras.

8
00:00:52.906 --> 00:01:02.684
At the bus stand, a free USB port can copy your data, or slip a harmful app onto your phone. Charge from a power socket, with your own adapter.

9
00:01:03.084 --> 00:01:09.781
O T means machines that run physical things: water pumps, lifts, factory machines, hospital equipment.

10
00:01:10.081 --> 00:01:18.505
A pump controller put online without protection can be stopped or misused. Tell the person in charge, and report to CERT-In and the police.

11
00:01:18.905 --> 00:01:26.148
If private footage leaks, report on cybercrime dot gov dot in, and call one one two if anyone's safety is at risk.

12
00:01:26.548 --> 00:01:31.410
Change the default, on day one. Charge from the plug, not the port.
